<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45309" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔτολμ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>brave-spirited,
			courageous</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ. ψυχῆς λῆμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simon.
					140
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπ᾽ εὐ. φρενός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1302
				</span></i>
			; of men, v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				1.7.4
			</span></i>, etc.: 
				Comp.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.122
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			, ib.<i><span class="en">
				68
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				6.14
			</span></i>, etc.: usu. in good sense, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ. εἶναι κρῖνε, τολμηρὸς δὲ μή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					<u>Mon.</u>
					153
				</span></i>
			, but iron., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ. ἰατρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					15.913
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύνες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>C.</u>
					3.383
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ. ἄκεα</span>
			<i>heroic</i> remedies, <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>CD</u>
				1.2
			</span></i>; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔτολμόν ἐστι</span> c.
				inf., <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>CA</u>
				2.1
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ εὔ. πρὸς τοὺς
			κινδύνους</span> Andronic.Rhod.<i><span class="en">
				p.576
			</span></i> M. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μως</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Tyrt.
				15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1298
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				17.34
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ότερον</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Sol.</u>
				14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>CA</u>
				1.1
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ότατα</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.461
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in bad
			sense, <i>daring, audacious, Anatolian Studies</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				204
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Termessus</span>).</div>
